#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:235
msgid "Prefixes and derivational suffixes are recognized"
msgstr "Prefixes and derivational suffixes are recognized"

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:237
msgid "A word that is flagged as a misspelling is re-read as a productive prefix (`sub-`, `semi-`, `non-`, `quasi-`, `counter-`, … — the full list is in `rust-core/dictionaries/affixes/prefixes.txt`) and/or a derivational suffix (`-ness`, `-ity`, `-able`, `-ly`, …) over a root. The root has to be a real word — one of yours, one from a bundled list, or one Harper knows — so `subalgebra` is accepted and `subxyzzy` is not. The closed and hyphenated spellings take the same path, because Harper and LanguageTool disagree about which one they report."
msgstr "A word that is flagged as a misspelling is re-read as a productive prefix (`sub-`, `semi-`, `non-`, `quasi-`, `counter-`, … — the full list is in `rust-core/dictionaries/affixes/prefixes.txt`) and/or a derivational suffix (`-ness`, `-ity`, `-able`, `-ly`, …) over a root. The root has to be a real word — one of yours, one from a bundled list, or one Harper knows — so `subalgebra` is accepted and `subxyzzy` is not. The closed and hyphenated spellings take the same path, because Harper and LanguageTool disagree about which one they report."

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:246
msgid "This is done by taking the word apart rather than by listing the results, because prefixes stack freely: the set of words `algebra` licenses is unbounded, so there is nothing to list."
msgstr "This is done by taking the word apart rather than by listing the results, because prefixes stack freely: the set of words `algebra` licenses is unbounded, so there is nothing to list."

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:250
msgid "Inflections are generated"
msgstr "Inflections are generated"

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:252
msgid "Plurals, and the past and progressive of `-ate`/`-ize`/`-ise`/`-ify` verbs, are generated from each dictionary word when the workspace loads and then matched like any other entry."
msgstr "Plurals, and the past and progressive of `-ate`/`-ize`/`-ise`/`-ify` verbs, are generated from each dictionary word when the workspace loads and then matched like any other entry."

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:256
msgid "Generated, not stripped, because the spelling rules only run one way. `occur` plus `-ed` is `occurred`; a checker that instead removed `-ed` from `occured` would find `occur` and accept a misspelling. The same shape accepts `childs` and `mouses`, which is why plurals are never recognized by taking a word apart."
msgstr "Generated, not stripped, because the spelling rules only run one way. `occur` plus `-ed` is `occurred`; a checker that instead removed `-ed` from `occured` would find `occur` and accept a misspelling. The same shape accepts `childs` and `mouses`, which is why plurals are never recognized by taking a word apart."

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:261
msgid "What keeps typos visible"
msgstr "What keeps typos visible"

#: ../../reference/config-schema.md:263
msgid "A decomposition on its own is weak evidence: `untill` reads as `un-` + `till`, and `till` really is a word. So the engine's own correction has the final say — if it can offer something one edit away from what you typed, the squiggle stays. A word with no plausible correction is what a genuine coinage looks like."
msgstr "A decomposition on its own is weak evidence: `untill` reads as `un-` + `till`, and `till` really is a word. So the engine's own correction has the final say — if it can offer something one edit away from what you typed, the squiggle stays. A word with no plausible correction is what a genuine coinage looks like."

